{"review_id":"205524324","date":"2017-10-22","comment":"The woodland cabin is so cosy and private. Despite atrocious weather we loved our stay and it must be truly stunning in better weather. Clean, stylish, cosy, personal touches and really welcoming hospitality. A small but gorgeous country retreat."}
{"review_id":"228584412","date":"2018-01-20","comment":"We really enjoyed our stay in this very cosy cabin, which was very well appointed with gadgets and various nice touches and had absolutely breathtaking views. It snowed while we were there which only made it more stunning!\nOn the way back in the evening we had to leave our car just down the road (not far at all!) And Nic was a fantastic help getting us back to it the next day.\nHighly recommended!"}
{"review_id":"247146163","date":"2018-03-27","comment":"Thank you Nic for being a fabulous host ! You were very flexible with your check in/out times for me and my partner. Your place is amazing and I wish we were able to spend a night there. Hopefully we come back soon! Xx"}
{"review_id":"325001490","date":"2018-09-18","comment":"It’s the perfect spot for a break from everything - so cozy, private and with stunning views! Upon entering the cottage you can see that Nic has thought of everything, you keep finding little details or things to make your stay better that I hadn’t thought of needing till I saw them! And the animals - so lovely, the adorable chickens and ducks running around the mini-private forest, and the ponies... I can’t recommend it enough! Brilliant stay in every aspect."}
{"review_id":"400862950","date":"2019-01-13","comment":"I booked the cabin as a Christmas present for my Mum and Dad, they absolutely loved it! They had an amazing time, and they were really pleased with the thoughtful touch of their names on the light box. Thank you Nic for being a lovely host!"}
{"review_id":"404505272","date":"2019-01-24","comment":"Great place, great cabin, great host!"}
{"review_id":"413294612","date":"2019-02-17","comment":"Beautiful house and area!"}
{"review_id":"544539430","date":"2019-10-10","comment":"Such a wonderful adventure for our family. Even though it rained, the setting was perfect to just huddle together and spend quality time. Nic’s hospitality was amazing, the little touches were brilliant. Finn loved the chickens running past and being able to see all sorts of wildlife.\nWhen it stopped raining we went for a lovely walk round for some dinner at The Cross Keys and also visited Grandpa Greens Ice Cream.\nAmazing! We will be back, either with or without the kids."}
{"review_id":"635883797","date":"2020-07-08","comment":"Amazing stay in a beautiful location, perfect little get away! The weather held out enough for us to have a BBQ the first night, and the second night we went to a nearby pub that was recommended which had great food! Loved having the chickens and ducks roaming around outside! Thoroughly enjoyed the whole experience."}
{"review_id":"730499215","date":"2021-02-12","comment":"Nic & Ian are incredibe host! They are genuine & super helpful - nothing was has been left to chance - our stay was just perfect! we would love to go back any time."}
{"review_id":"478068877773949443","date":"2021-10-21","comment":"We had a wonderful time at the cabin! The facilities were great, it was really well located and we loved Nic’s s super helpful guidebook! We will definitely be recommending it to friends!"}
{"review_id":"533866560913419760","date":"2022-01-06","comment":"We had a wonderful time , great host and a truly lovely spot . There are also some fantastic walks and villages near the accommodation . We will be definitely be going back .\nMark and Katie"}
{"review_id":"612867498879893442","date":"2022-04-25","comment":"We had a lovely stay at this retreat. Myself, my husband and my 8 year old daughter stayed to celebrate his 40th birthday.\nNic was very accomodating and the gift of eggs and milk was so thoughtful. Sitting around the firepit was a treat and in the cabin you can see rabbits, horses, birds and pheasants. The family cat absolutely made our holiday and we were happy to accomodate her in the day as we are huge cat fans.\nA beautiful short walk to the local pubs. A short drive to local villages and Huddersfield isn't too far away either.\nWe stayed for 3 nights. We took ready cooked curry and bolognaise to heat in the microwave and had a little BBQ on the firepit one night. we didn't use the fryer but it seemed very versatile.\nI've had to send out this location and booking details to at least 6 of my friends as they all want to stay too!\nThanks again xxx"}
{"review_id":"791925638372478054","date":"2022-12-28","comment":"A very cosy place!"}
{"review_id":"924550870019941067","date":"2023-06-29","comment":"Lovely little peaceful place in beautiful surroundings, Nic was a great host who was very helpful. Will definitely be revisiting again next year."}
{"review_id":"925906170321238358","date":"2023-07-01","comment":"An amazing stay! Very chilled out getaway. Well worth a stay."}
{"review_id":"941929356308426033","date":"2023-07-23","comment":"Lovely place, with beautiful views. Very peaceful."}
{"review_id":"951325391772625942","date":"2023-08-05","comment":"We had a lovely peaceful stay. The place was cosy and comfortable with beautiful surroundings. We enjoyed it very much!"}
{"review_id":"968739264386022337","date":"2023-08-29","comment":"We booked this as a last minute get away from London and it couldn't have been more perfect! The cosy cabin has everything you could want/ need for a few days away, and Nic has made some wonderfully thoughtful touches. The weather held out, so we were able to enjoy a bbq and fire pit one night. There are some beautiful walks from the door as well as local pubs. We had a wonderful time and highly recommend a stay here"}
{"review_id":"1007112355435305409","date":"2023-10-21","comment":"The perfect getaway if you need a relaxing break. The location is amazing and private. Nic is a lovely host, very responsive."}
{"review_id":"1016560281345504600","date":"2023-11-03","comment":"Beautiful place. Nic was a great host. Great location. Thank you"}
{"review_id":"1080420804129944026","date":"2024-01-30","comment":"The romantic cabin in Diggle is a dreamy retreat for a short holiday, boasting a cozy ambiance and tranquil surroundings. The attentive hosts ensure a warm welcome and are quick to respond to any inquiries, ensuring a seamless experience. The cabin is equipped with modern amenities, providing comfort and convenience throughout your stay. Nestled amidst nature, it sets the stage for intimate moments and peaceful relaxation, making it a perfect getaway for couples seeking a romantic escape in Diggle."}
{"review_id":"1113040015611101925","date":"2024-03-15","comment":"Amazing stay, really nice lodge and so relaxing!"}
{"review_id":"1143377325560903608","date":"2024-04-26","comment":"Truly beautiful! The lodge was spotless, great location and very peaceful. We got the train into Greenfield and it was a 10min Uber ride from the station itself. Very easy to locate even if you’re not driving. Lovely walks close by. I wish we booked more than 2 nights, I would’ve happily stayed longer. Nic is also very responsive and helpful."}
{"review_id":"1148491245401563608","date":"2024-05-03","comment":"Excellent stay, would really recommend to others as a little getaway with your partner."}
{"review_id":"1170219401413436816","date":"2024-06-02","comment":"Such a great get away, enjoyed every minute! The cabin is as described. The local area is amazing, the views are incredible which create great walks. The food in the local area is spot on with a great night life! Thanks Nic!"}
{"review_id":"1175333299408180726","date":"2024-06-09","comment":"Your own slice of heaven for a stay in a cosy cabin. Loved looking up into the canopy of the trees whilst lying in bed! Absolutely beautiful!"}
{"review_id":"1199256482012386702","date":"2024-07-12","comment":"Absolutely perfect in every way.\nThe place was as described, if not even better.\nThe views were amazing and we really felt in our own private little world.\nNic was very proactive with communication and making sure we had all the information we needed to find the place and get in.\nA short walk into Diggle (though a bit steep on the way back) which was a wonderful little town. Make sure you go for brunch at The Diggle Lock."}
{"review_id":"1233299527596453561","date":"2024-08-28","comment":"Was a great getaway from the city. 45 min drive away from Manchester means that there are always places to go, eat, activities etc. Great location and felt super safe which is always good. Perfect if you like walks, hikes, runs and that sort of stuff. Would definitely recommend :)"}
{"review_id":"1248488961365430734","date":"2024-09-18","comment":"This airbnb was amazing and we felt at home. The house was super cozy and the view was great especially in the mornings. Amazing farmland and animals, made a chicken friend(we called it Darren). Left feeling refreshed and happy, will definitely come back soon for longer 🙂 Thanks Nic"}
{"review_id":"1253519732790786852","date":"2024-09-25","comment":"It is a lovely and charming location to reside in. My fiancee and I had a wonderful time there. I wholeheartedly endorse this location for couples."}
{"review_id":"1256491206711237639","date":"2024-09-29","comment":"Fabulous stay and had everything we needed. We will be back!"}
{"review_id":"1281126191347015427","date":"2024-11-02","comment":"Absolutely stunning location, went during autumn scenery all around was stunning and cabin was lovely and cosy. Lots of good local ammenities and the host was flawless. Great communication and very hospitable. Few animals about the farm grounds, was great to open the blinds to the resident chicken"}
{"review_id":"1313789858180875300","date":"2024-12-17","comment":"Brilliant place .. felt right at home. Beautiful spot .. would go again"}
{"review_id":"1316647204971148311","date":"2024-12-21","comment":"Beautiful stay during stormy season - i would certainly visit again to see it during the other seasons. The farm ducks are a firm favourite!"}
{"review_id":"1342730498615871175","date":"2025-01-26","comment":"Beautiful stay, the tiny home was so cosy and peaceful, the views were the most special thing to be able to wake up to! We loved our stay, we were gutted we couldn’t stay longer, there were so many walking trails and nice little towny centres to visit; We were looking at Nic’s other listings to come back to before we had even left!"}
{"review_id":"1368066204141009684","date":"2025-03-02","comment":"Lovely place"}
{"review_id":"1370319234852949149","date":"2025-03-05","comment":"We had the most amazing stay. Arrived at night time so woke up in the morning to the most incredible views.\nThe lodge was beautiful. And incredibly clean.\nNic was wonderful. Always there to answer any questions we had.\nWe would most definitely go back."}
{"review_id":"1382653027083381418","date":"2025-03-22","comment":"I had a lovely stay, the kitchen is well stocked if you’re wanting to do some of your own cooking. There are plently of walks surrounding and a helpful book with trails.\nOverall it’s decorated beautifully and the location is just stunning."}
{"review_id":"1431164087108783128","date":"2025-05-28","comment":"A beautiful cottage with everything you could need. Very clean and Jayne was very thoughtful throughout."}
{"review_id":"1447836530805707486","date":"2025-06-20","comment":"lovely views and a great stay, would love to go back xx"}
{"review_id":"1452907371909929425","date":"2025-06-27","comment":"We had an amazing stay at the lodge. Beautiful surroundings and wildlife. Nic was a great host and was so accommodating from the start. Would highly recommend for a peaceful getaway!!!"}
{"review_id":"1454369477206740947","date":"2025-06-29","comment":"Had the most perfect stay. Exactly as described and super lovely. The short walk to the lodge from the car is just adorable in itself. Beautifully clean and stocked with all amenities we hope to return again soon, it was a brilliant break."}
{"review_id":"1455750130871851206","date":"2025-07-01","comment":"Absolutely perfect. The lodge itself is beautiful with everything you need. Clean and tidy. Very private and peaceful. Loved everything about it. The view from the lodge is stunning. Would definitely recommend. Can't wait to visit again in the future"}
{"review_id":"1467414777650332636","date":"2025-07-17","comment":"Lovely stay and would recommend to anyone. Our second time visiting Nic’s places and they have been great!"}
{"review_id":"1477459781241616784","date":"2025-07-31","comment":"We had a beautiful stay at the cabin in the woods. Cabin was stunning, the location was peaceful, we had everything we needed and the wildlife was amazing to watch. Nic was also an amazing host and the communication / thought that went into making sure we enjoyed our stay was 10/10. Highly recommend!"}
{"review_id":"1508668535406918240","date":"2025-09-12","comment":"I had an amazing stay! The place was spotless, beautifully decorated, and exactly as described in the listing. check-in was super easy. The location was perfect-close to everything needed but still quiet and relaxing. The little touches, like the little sweeet treats and fresh flowers really made me feel at home. I loved watching the horses in the field while enjoying a cup of tea in the morning. I'd absolutely stay here again and highly recommend it to anyone visiting the area!"}
{"review_id":"1522456158441107084","date":"2025-10-01","comment":"Myself and my partner had an amazing stay! Nic even shown us her horses which was lovely! All round great place to stay would recommend staying here 10/10"}
{"review_id":"1523867399539256990","date":"2025-10-03","comment":"Amazing lodge, clean and exactly as decribed. The views are lovely. Nic was super helpful and nice. Already planning my next visit.\nWill highly recommend!"}
{"review_id":"1530416978350802990","date":"2025-10-12","comment":"We had such a wonderful stay, so peaceful and incredible views. The property itself was super cosy, clean and had everything we could have needed.\nIt's very well located to go exploring, and there are some fantastic local places to eat.\nNic was a fantastic host, and very kindly introduced us to her horses (the highlight of the trip). We will absolutely be returning!"}
{"review_id":"1534086878231585044","date":"2025-10-17","comment":"Loved this romantic lodge, it has everything, cozy, pretty, warm, the views are just stunning. We sat outside on a cool October night, roaring fire in the fire pit, blankets, hot water bottles, pub quiz, wine, music, I think it was one of the best nights ever! Thank you ❤️"}
{"review_id":"1536966519758577462","date":"2025-10-21","comment":"Really special place. Beautiful for walking but the weather was poor whilst I was there. So used it has a peaceful relaxing retreat. It was perfect. Nice local pubs to visit too. Superb haven . With wonderful views.will definitely return in another season. My new retreat when life gets stressful."}
{"review_id":"1541299966220526901","date":"2025-10-27","comment":"Gorgeous little bolthole. Amazing views! Loved the extra treats from Nic - very nice touch. We had a super relaxing break here. Many thanks"}
{"review_id":"1546386032852321422","date":"2025-11-03","comment":"Nic was an amazing host. She made us feel right at home. She is very responsive and made sure that we were having the best time and gave us amazing recommendations on where to go. I would say that every penny spent was very worth it and I would definitely come again. Thank you Nic for everything 💗🙏🏻"}
{"review_id":"1555059752991075210","date":"2025-11-15","comment":"A beautiful lodge in a beautiful location.\nAfter enquiring if an earlier check in would be possible due to our engagements for the day, Nic accommodated us and got us an earlier check in.\nEverything in the lodge was perfect.\nHeating was on, a bottle of wine and flowers on the table, and everything looked immaculate.\nWhilst out a power cut hit due to a storm bringing down a power line and Nic messaged to let us know.\nShe arranged for an emergency repair worker to be out the next morning, got us candles, torches, lights, and even an emergency phone charger.\nShe waited up for us to get back even though it was late.\nThe next morning she went out and brought us hot drinks, breakfast and bottled water.\nDue to it being so cold she then arranged for us to move to another cottage close by that hadn’t been affected by the power cut and refunded us our second nights stay.\nShe was so friendly, helpful, went above and beyond anything we expected. We’ll definitely be going back again"}
{"review_id":"1567362488096554549","date":"2025-12-02","comment":"My partner and I have just stayed for 2 nights at Nic’s place. The lodge was so clean and comfortable. The weather was terrible on one of the days so it would have been so easy to stay and be cosy but we braved one of the local walks recommended by Nic and we were so glad that we did.\nA beautiful space and we would definitely come back again."}
{"review_id":"1576119731598752249","date":"2025-12-14","comment":"Beautiful surroundings and a great location. This cabin was cosy and comfortable."}
{"review_id":"1580479819728366829","date":"2025-12-20","comment":"Super cozy and beautiful place! The view is soo good!! Hopefully I can be back in summer!"}
{"review_id":"1604438700079681265","date":"2026-01-22","comment":"We loved staying at The Cabin! It is so gorgeous, the surroundings are beautiful and Nic thought of everything!"}
{"review_id":"1605797246270059351","date":"2026-01-24","comment":"This is our second stay at the lodge; literally a year apart! My wife and I loved the place as we reminisced the place and wanted to come back. The cold is different up north compared to the midlands but the views just warm you up. At peace! The lodge is small but cozy for a couple. It has the essentials but do grab extra layers for winter as the kitchen/ bathroom can get very cold. Nic is such a lovely host and very responsive. She makes you feel welcomed to her premises. We would defo stay here again!"}
{"review_id":"1623943881966409953","date":"2026-02-18","comment":"What a wonderful place to stay! We had the most amazing time and Nic is a fantastic host! She is responsive and made sure we were well looked after.\nThe highlight of our trip is definitely the visit we had from the sheep along with waking up to the stunning views straight from your bed!\nThe lodge is perfectly thought out with everything you need for a fantastic stay and the guide book with recommendations was fantastic just a shame we didn’t have time to do all the great recommendations!\nWe would love to be back!\nThank you Nic"}
{"review_id":"1639862453542087978","date":"2026-03-12","comment":"We had a lovely stay! The lodge is so cozy, tidy and had everything we needed. We loved waking up to the gorgeous view, and the fire pit was an added bonus!\nNic even left us a note and some prosecco to help us celebrate our anniversary which was such a thoughtful touch. She is very friendly and easy to communicate with.\nWe also loved the little book with local recommendations for food/drinks which helped us decide where to go.\nWe would definitely stay again, thanks for having us!"}
{"review_id":"1662282666057095192","date":"2026-04-12","comment":"Home from such a lovely weekend away. The lodge had been in one of my 'dream stays' folder on air b&b for a while so I was so excited to finally be visiting! It did not disappoint! Absolutely stunning views and beautifully decorated lodge! It was local to shops but was so peaceful where it was situated. We would 100% be back! We loved watching the horses! Nic was also a great host - fast and efficient! We got a bit lost on arrival but we rang Nic and she helped direct us! Thank you so much for having us! The little touches on arrival were also very kind! ❤️"}
{"review_id":"1665925640288501721","date":"2026-04-17","comment":"Beautiful place to stay, amazing views and very private. Nic was a lovely host, very responsive and had set up the lodge very thoughtfully, and the welcome guide was extremely helpful and informative.\nWe enjoyed a lovely hike with breathtaking views, a day out to the heights of Abraham and a couple of restaurants all recommended by Nic. One day we spent most of the day in the lodge and enjoyed the insane views made even better by horses galloping and playing in the fields just in front.\nWould definitely recommend! 5 stars!"}
{"review_id":"1673167549104105339","date":"2026-04-27","comment":"Had a lovely relaxing stay in the most beautiful peaceful surroundings absolute gem of a place, carefully planned to be special but with everything needed at hand.\nThank you for a lovely stay x"}
{"review_id":"1680480597319919042","date":"2026-05-07","comment":"Absolutely gorgeous, peaceful location. Perfect hideaway for a couple of days with such beautiful views, we didn’t want to leave!\nWe just relaxed, watched the horses and pheasants right outside and listened to the birds.\nThere’s everything you need inside - kitchen facilities to cook, smart TV and lovely little touches like gowns, sweet treats and hot water bottle.\nWe went out to a lovely local pub one night, the Cross Keys and were even more delighted when we got a 10% discount for staying in the lodge. So make sure you tell them! They have good food and peacocks in the garden.\nAlso walked to Grandpa Greene’s which is a must for ice cream and other food.\nNic was a great host, quickly replying to messages while allowing us to feel like we had our own space and privacy.\nWe’d love to escape here again some time❤️"}
{"review_id":"1684834583629241490","date":"2026-05-13","comment":"This place was wasted on me a little as I stayed for one night while in the area on business. It is an amazing place that needs to be enjoyed over a few days at least. The location is incredible with breathtaking views. The accommodation is perfect. Incredibly well presented and luxurious. Everything you could want for a long weekend is provided - there was even a massive selection of DVDs to watch incase the weather lets you down. I strongly recommend staying here but you need at least 3 nights to fully enjoy it and the surrounding area."}
{"review_id":"1693468294679772153","date":"2026-05-25","comment":"Wow, What a lovely place to stay! We had the most amazing bank holiday weekend here and had the best weather to match!!\nNic was so lovely and helped out whenever we needed.\nSitting and having a BBQ watching the horses and overlooking the views is something I will always remember!"}
{"review_id":"1694898892109174709","date":"2026-05-27","comment":"Lovely place to stay, everything we needed was there. 10 minutes walk to pubs with gorgeous food.\nSo relaxing and spectacular views, will definitely be coming back!"}
{"review_id":"1707999240236020704","date":"2026-06-14","comment":"We loved our stay, exactly what was needed after a very stressful week! Such a nice surprise to have a bottle of fizz in the fridge for our arrival… it was opened immediately!\nThe surroundings are beautiful and an amazing view out of the bi-fold doors - great on both mornings and evenings.\nPlace had everything for our short stay, just a shame we didn’t get time to enjoy the outdoor log fire. Next time!"}

