{"review_id":"449811320722078668","date":"2021-09-12","comment":"We stayed with Pillo Rooms for 2 nights.\nWhilst the apartment itself was largely fine and true to the pictures (the bathroom and kitchen were fairly decent), we had a very bad experience with the inflexibility around check in/check out time.\nWe booked the apartment about 2 weeks in advance of our stay. When we informed the company we would be travelling to Manchester from London after work, and that we’d resultantly need to collect the keys late in the evening, we were told the ‘latest check in slot that was available was 5 pm.’ After several messages back and forth, Pillo Rooms would not budge and told us we absolutely could not check in any later. I ended up having to take a half day from work, and rush down to Manchester on the train. When I got to Manchester I grabbed a cab but unfortunately there was heavy traffic so my ETA was going to be a few minutes outside of the 15 minute slot. I had to call Pillo Rooms and practically beg them on the phone not to leave. I was concerned my friends and I would literally have nowhere to stay for the night otherwise, and I noted I was only 2 mins away according to the cab driver. I pulled up just in time before the company contact left.\nIt was so stressful and later confusing as the company representative stated they would have ‘had to push my time slot back’ had I not made it (and if I hadn’t made it this would only have been by a minute or 2.) This completely disagreed with what Pillo Rooms initially told me, which was that a 5pm slot was the absolute latest they could offer.\nThe reason an in-person check in was required is also beyond me. Anything I was shown could have easily been written down. My id/ the form you have to fill in could easily have been scanned and sent in advance. A key safe where we could have retrieved the keys at a suitable time would have been so much simpler.\nAdditionally, you’re supposed to be able to organise a ‘late’ check out for a small fee. When we requested this, again we were told this wasn’t possible as other people were checking into the apartment later that day…\nEverything we requested was basically refused and completely on Pillo Rooms terms - no flexibility or consideration given to the guests. When my friend realised she’d left her jumper in the apartment, we messaged asking if they could possibly post it back to us in London (we’d have covered the costs.) Pillo Rooms informed us she’d have 7 days to come to Manchester to collect it.\nThe service absolutely was not ‘luxury’. None of the touches you’d expect in a ‘luxury’ apartment were there - there wasn’t even olive oil, salt, pepper etc left in the kitchen to cook with, it was completely bare. The TV also did not properly work, but we didn’t bother flagging this at the time as we spent most of the weekend outside the apartment anyway.\nThe location, though close to the centre which was good, was a bit ropey and I wouldn’t have felt comfortable walking out at night on my own.\nOverall it was not a good experience and unfortunately I would not stay with Pillo Rooms again."}
{"review_id":"556403007702776947","date":"2022-02-06","comment":"1)More information about how to get to this place the Sat navs all thee of them car plus two phones did not recognise where this place was not just for me but for a friend of mine who tried to visit he also could not find it. Very misleading and not what I would call near to the Centre of Manchester it’s way out!! I spent an hour and a quarter trying to get there after a 3hr 45 mins up from London not what you need when the following day was a 6.30 am start.\n2) location was grubby dirty and we felt unsafe walking out to try and get food with people harassing us and making us head back towards apartment.\n2) the bathroom is decorated well but the mirror cabinet is set for people who are 5’10 and above so you can’t see in the mirror if you are 5’4 or below.\n3) the double bed was so bad I didn’t sleep as the springs were sticking up in my back through the mattress you could actually feel the wire. So no sleep!!!\n3) The TV was pixilated and you could not watch it.\n4) little hand paper towels to dry the plates and knives and forks was ridiculous. A tea cloth is not a luxury!!!\n4) the noise level in the corridor of people coming and going and shouting at high levels was echoing and loud. Some dampener on the main door or on the floors would be advisable. Seeing as the bed is right by the door.\n5) rubbish all over roads does not present a good look. Very tacky and does not make you feel welcome.\n6) couldn’t wait to check out so on Saturday we checked out as soon as we could I was not going to stay another night in this duplex.\nA mattress was left in the corridor in plastic the next day. I assume I was supposed to carry it in and change it? No note on that.\n7) Tried messaging on my way to apartment to see if I could get any more information to no response.\nI very nearly checked into a hotel it was that frustrating!!!\nAnyway as I said before I will expect some compensation. This is the worst case scenario air BnB I’ve encountered.\n7 people were asked if they knew where Derby st was only the last person was luckily able to help thankfully!!! They had worked there. NOT FOR ME!!!"}
{"review_id":"584580740310203359","date":"2022-03-17","comment":"Fantastic location, clean and modern. Would stay here again and we shall…"}
{"review_id":"658574185996192415","date":"2022-06-27","comment":"Stunning little apartment just outside of the city centre. The place was so clean and had excellent facilities and communication was great. The only fault I have with the place is the lack of air con as it was very hot and there was only one fan and it was quite difficult to get to sleep with how hot it was"}
{"review_id":"659938496401713198","date":"2022-06-29","comment":"Would definitely stay again when in Manchester, great location clean plenty of towels and a great shower!"}
