{"review_id":"893364987834324271","date":"2023-05-17","comment":"Great stay, nice people thankyou :)"}
{"review_id":"903513388036904021","date":"2023-05-31","comment":"I had a lovely and comfortable stay at Nicole's . Highly recommended!\nThe neighbourhood was great, calm, had good access to public transports (very close to 2 two bus stops while tram station was in walking distance) thus easy access to city centre and airport. The self-check in process was clear and easy. Nicole was kind enough to let me put my lugage in her place prior my check in time, which was very helpful since I arrived in the morning!\nMy room was on the 3rd floor next to the bathroom. It was a clean, compact, comfortable, warm room with a window for air circulation. The bed and bedding were comfortable. The bathroom and kitchen were clean with good facilities and amenities as described and available to use. The accomodation is very affordable and valuable in terms of the price.\nNicole is a nice, communicative, friendly and helpful host while giving me privacy. She gladly helped me to settle in. I stayed there for 12 days and enjoy every moment of my stay there :)"}
{"review_id":"906332685519942953","date":"2023-06-04","comment":"I felt very welcome and the location was perfect for going to a gig at the Emirates Old Trafford. I would come again!"}
{"review_id":"921602515334372551","date":"2023-06-25","comment":"Although small, the room was clean and cosy and a good base for the week. I found it easy to get into Manchester and to Salford Quays - good nearby transport.\nNicole was a great host - friendly and full of ideas of places to see during the visit. Thank you, Nicole & Andrew!!"}
{"review_id":"929534346832936133","date":"2023-07-06","comment":"First class Pillows and beddings and a kind cool host. I highly recommend Nicole's place."}
{"review_id":"943413848234265397","date":"2023-07-25","comment":"Great place to stay"}
{"review_id":"968000245269639483","date":"2023-08-28","comment":"I stayed in Manchester for 2 weeks, at Nicole's place. She is wonderful, always responsive, friendly, and positive. It was great to interact with her. The place was a good place, in a good area. I personally don't know how to judge the quality of sites in the UK, but the location *felt* right. It did not feel ominous.\nCheck-in was straightforward. The rooms are simple but adequate. If I had to nitpick, I would say that the bed size (width, height, and length) was a bit large. I say this because the bed took up to 70% of the room. It was also quite soft for my comfort which did affect my ability to sleep well, to a degree. I wish the room was decorated with a table and chair.\nThe kitchen and living room were downstairs. They are joined and are relatively spacious. It felt good going downstairs. The only gripe I would have is that if the hosts had a plan to watch TV or a movie in the living room, it meant you couldn't do anything besides stay in your room.\nI recommend this listing!"}
